## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to integrate per-tenant manifests with React concurrent rendering patterns, while ensuring minimal re-renders and clean switch semantics.

## Key Concepts
- useSyncExternalStore for per-tenant streams
- memoization via Map keyed by (tenantId, widgetId)
- React.lazy + Suspense for dynamic widgets
- React.memo to prevent unnecessary renders

## Code Example
```javascript
// sketch: memoized prop selector
const propCache = new Map();
function getWidgetProps(tenantId, widgetId, manifest, globalProps){
  const key = `${tenantId}::${widgetId}`;
  if (propCache.has(key)) return propCache.get(key);
  const w = manifest.widgets.find(w => w.id===widgetId);
  const props = { ...globalProps, ...w?.props };
  propCache.set(key, props);
  return props;
}
```

